#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:2
msgid "Basics of libuv"
msgstr "libuv 基础"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:4
msgid ""
"libuv enforces an **asynchronous**, **event-driven** style of "
"programming.  Its core job is to provide an event loop and callback based"
" notifications of I/O and other activities.  libuv offers core utilities "
"like timers, non-blocking networking support, asynchronous file system "
"access, child processes and more."
msgstr "libuv 强制采用 **异步**、**事件驱动** 的编程风格。其核心任务是提供事件循环，以及基于回调的 I/O 和其他活动的通知。libuv 提供定时器、非阻塞网络支持、异步文件系统访问、子进程等核心工具。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:10
msgid "Event loops"
msgstr "事件循环"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:12
msgid ""
"In event-driven programming, an application expresses interest in certain"
" events and respond to them when they occur. The responsibility of "
"gathering events from the operating system or monitoring other sources of"
" events is handled by libuv, and the user can register callbacks to be "
"invoked when an event occurs. The event-loop usually keeps running "
"*forever*. In pseudocode:"
msgstr "在事件驱动编程中，应用程序表达对某些事件的关注，并在事件发生时作出响应。从操作系统收集事件或监视其他事件来源的职责由 libuv 承担，用户可以注册回调，使其在事件发生时被调用。事件循环通常会 *永远* 运行下去。伪代码如下："

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:25
msgid "Some examples of events are:"
msgstr "以下是一些事件的例子："

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:27
msgid "File is ready for writing"
msgstr "文件已准备好写入"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:28
msgid "A socket has data ready to be read"
msgstr "套接字有数据可供读取"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:29
msgid "A timer has timed out"
msgstr "定时器已超时"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:31
msgid ""
"This event loop is encapsulated by ``uv_run()`` -- the end-all function "
"when using libuv."
msgstr "这个事件循环由 ``uv_run()`` 封装——它是使用 libuv 时最核心的函数。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:34
msgid ""
"The most common activity of systems programs is to deal with input and "
"output, rather than a lot of number-crunching. The problem with using "
"conventional input/output functions (``read``, ``fprintf``, etc.) is that"
" they are **blocking**. The actual write to a hard disk or reading from a"
" network, takes a disproportionately long time compared to the speed of "
"the processor. The functions don't return until the task is done, so that"
" your program is doing nothing. For programs which require high "
"performance this is a major roadblock as other activities and other I/O "
"operations are kept waiting."
msgstr "系统程序最常见的活动是处理输入输出，而不是做大量的数值计算。使用常规输入/输出函数（``read``、``fprintf`` 等）的问题在于它们是 **阻塞** 的。实际写入硬盘或从网络读取，与处理器的速度相比，耗时长得不成比例。这些函数在任务完成之前不会返回，期间你的程序无事可做。对于要求高性能的程序来说，这是一大障碍，因为其他活动和其他 I/O 操作都只能等待。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:43
msgid ""
"One of the standard solutions is to use threads. Each blocking I/O "
"operation is started in a separate thread (or in a thread pool). When the"
" blocking function gets invoked in the thread, the operating system can "
"schedule another thread to run, which actually needs the CPU."
msgstr "标准解决方案之一是使用线程。每个阻塞式 I/O 操作都在单独的线程（或线程池）中启动。当阻塞函数在线程中被调用时，操作系统可以调度另一个线程来运行，这个线程才是真正需要 CPU 的。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:48
msgid ""
"The approach followed by libuv uses another style, which is the "
"**asynchronous, non-blocking** style. Most modern operating systems "
"provide event notification subsystems. For example, a normal ``read`` "
"call on a socket would block until the sender actually sent something. "
"Instead, the application can request the operating system to watch the "
"socket and put an event notification in the queue. The application can "
"inspect the events at its convenience (perhaps doing some number "
"crunching before to use the processor to the maximum) and grab the data. "
"It is **asynchronous** because the application expressed interest at one "
"point, then used the data at another point (in time and space). It is "
"**non-blocking** because the application process was free to do other "
"tasks. This fits in well with libuv's event-loop approach, since the "
"operating system events can be treated as just another libuv event. The "
"non-blocking ensures that other events can continue to be handled as fast"
" as they come in [#]_."
msgstr "libuv 采用的是另一种风格，即 **异步、非阻塞** 风格。大多数现代操作系统都提供事件通知子系统。例如，对套接字进行普通的 ``read`` 调用会一直阻塞，直到发送方真正发送了数据。应用程序可以改为请求操作系统监视该套接字，并把事件通知放入队列。应用程序可以在方便的时候检查这些事件（也许事先做一些数值计算，把处理器用到极致），然后取走数据。说它是 **异步** 的，是因为应用程序在一个时点表达了关注，然后在另一个时点（时间和空间上）使用数据。说它是 **非阻塞** 的，是因为应用程序进程可以自由地执行其他任务。这与 libuv 的事件循环方式非常契合，因为操作系统事件可以看作只是又一种 libuv 事件。非阻塞确保其他事件可以在到达时持续得到尽快处理 [#]_。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:64
msgid ""
"How the I/O is run in the background is not of our concern, but due to "
"the way our computer hardware works, with the thread as the basic unit of"
" the processor, libuv and OSes will usually run background/worker threads"
" and/or polling to perform tasks in a non-blocking manner."
msgstr "I/O 在后台如何运行并不是我们所关心的，但由于计算机硬件的工作方式——线程是处理器的基本单位——libuv 和各操作系统通常会运行后台/工作线程和/或进行轮询，以非阻塞的方式执行任务。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:69
msgid ""
"Bert Belder, one of the libuv core developers, has a small video "
"explaining the architecture of libuv and its background. If you have no "
"prior experience with libuv, it is a quick, useful watch."
msgstr "libuv 核心开发者之一 Bert Belder 有一个小视频，讲解了 libuv 的架构及其背景。如果你此前没有接触过 libuv，这个视频简短实用，值得一看。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:73
msgid ""
"libuv's event loop is explained in more detail in the `documentation "
"<https://docs.libuv.org/en/v1.x/design.html#the-i-o-loop>`_."
msgstr "libuv 的事件循环在 `文档 <https://docs.libuv.org/en/v1.x/design.html#the-i-o-loop>`_ 中有更详细的讲解。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:83
msgid "Hello World"
msgstr "Hello World"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:85
msgid ""
"With the basics out of the way, let's write our first libuv program. It "
"does nothing, except start a loop which will exit immediately."
msgstr "掌握了基础知识之后，我们来编写第一个 libuv 程序。它什么也不做，只是启动一个会立即退出的事件循环。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:88
msgid "helloworld/main.c"
msgstr "helloworld/main.c"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:93
msgid ""
"This program quits immediately because it has no events to process. A "
"libuv event loop has to be told to watch out for events using the various"
" API functions."
msgstr "这个程序会立即退出，因为它没有要处理的事件。必须通过各种各样的 API 函数告诉 libuv 事件循环去留意事件。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:97
msgid ""
"Starting with libuv v1.0, users should allocate the memory for the loops "
"before initializing it with ``uv_loop_init(uv_loop_t *)``. This allows "
"you to plug in custom memory management. Remember to de-initialize the "
"loop using ``uv_loop_close(uv_loop_t *)`` and then delete the storage. "
"The examples never close loops since the program quits after the loop "
"ends and the system will reclaim memory. Production grade projects, "
"especially long running systems programs, should take care to release "
"correctly."
msgstr "从 libuv v1.0 开始，用户应当先为事件循环分配内存，然后用 ``uv_loop_init(uv_loop_t *)`` 初始化它。这样你就可以接入自定义的内存管理。请记得使用 ``uv_loop_close(uv_loop_t *)`` 反初始化循环，然后再释放存储空间。这些示例从不关闭事件循环，因为程序在循环结束之后就退出了，系统会回收内存。生产级项目，尤其是长期运行的系统程序，应当注意正确地释放。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:106
msgid "Default loop"
msgstr "默认事件循环"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:108
msgid ""
"A default loop is provided by libuv and can be accessed using "
"``uv_default_loop()``. You should use this loop if you only want a single"
" loop."
msgstr "libuv 提供了一个默认事件循环，可以通过 ``uv_default_loop()`` 访问。如果你只需要单个事件循环，就应当使用这个循环。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:112
msgid "default-loop/main.c"
msgstr "default-loop/main.c"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:119
msgid ""
"node.js uses the default loop as its main loop. If you are writing "
"bindings you should be aware of this."
msgstr "node.js 使用默认事件循环作为其主循环。如果你在编写绑定，应当注意这一点。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:125
msgid "Error handling"
msgstr "错误处理"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:127
msgid ""
"Initialization functions or synchronous functions which may fail return a"
" negative number on error. Async functions that may fail will pass a "
"status parameter to their callbacks. The error messages are defined as "
"``UV_E*`` `constants`_."
msgstr "可能失败的初始化函数或同步函数在出错时返回负数。可能失败的异步函数会向其回调传递一个状态参数。错误信息定义为 ``UV_E*`` `constants`_。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:131
msgid ""
"You can use the ``uv_strerror(int)`` and ``uv_err_name(int)`` functions "
"to get a ``const char *`` describing the error or the error name "
"respectively."
msgstr "你可以使用 ``uv_strerror(int)`` 和 ``uv_err_name(int)`` 函数，分别获取描述错误的 ``const char *`` 和错误名称。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:134
msgid ""
"I/O read callbacks (such as for files and sockets) are passed a parameter"
" ``nread``. If ``nread`` is less than 0, there was an error (UV_EOF is "
"the end of file error, which you may want to handle differently)."
msgstr "I/O 读取回调（例如针对文件和套接字的回调）会收到一个参数 ``nread``。如果 ``nread`` 小于 0，则说明发生了错误（UV_EOF 是文件结束错误，你可能需要以不同的方式处理它）。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:137
msgid "Handles and Requests"
msgstr "句柄与请求"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:139
msgid ""
"libuv works by the user expressing interest in particular events. This is"
" usually done by creating a **handle** to an I/O device, timer or "
"process. Handles are opaque structs named as ``uv_TYPE_t`` where type "
"signifies what the handle is used for."
msgstr "libuv 的工作方式是让用户表达对特定事件的关注。这通常通过为 I/O 设备、定时器或进程创建 **句柄** 来完成。句柄是命名为 ``uv_TYPE_t`` 的不透明结构体，其中的 type 表明该句柄的用途。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:144
msgid "libuv watchers"
msgstr "libuv 监视器"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:189
msgid ""
"Handles represent long-lived objects. Async operations on such handles "
"are identified using **requests**. A request is short-lived (usually used"
" across only one callback) and usually indicates one I/O operation on a "
"handle. Requests are used to preserve context between the initiation and "
"the callback of individual actions. For example, an UDP socket is "
"represented by a ``uv_udp_t``, while individual writes to the socket use "
"a ``uv_udp_send_t`` structure that is passed to the callback after the "
"write is done."
msgstr "句柄代表长寿命的对象。此类句柄上的异步操作通过 **请求** 来标识。请求是短寿命的（通常只在单个回调中使用），通常表示对句柄的一次 I/O 操作。请求用于在各个动作的发起与回调之间保存上下文。例如，UDP 套接字由 ``uv_udp_t`` 表示，而对套接字的每次写入则使用 ``uv_udp_send_t`` 结构，写入完成后该结构会被传递给回调。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:197
msgid "Handles are setup by a corresponding::"
msgstr "设置句柄用的是相应的："

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:201
msgid "function."
msgstr "函数。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:203
msgid ""
"Callbacks are functions which are called by libuv whenever an event the "
"watcher is interested in has taken place. Application specific logic will"
" usually be implemented in the callback. For example, an IO watcher's "
"callback will receive the data read from a file, a timer callback will be"
" triggered on timeout and so on."
msgstr "回调是当监视器所关注的事件发生时由 libuv 调用的函数。应用特定的逻辑通常会在回调中实现。例如，IO 监视器的回调会接收从文件中读取的数据，定时器回调会在超时时被触发，诸如此类。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:210
msgid "Idling"
msgstr "空转"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:212
msgid ""
"Here is an example of using an idle handle. The callback is called once "
"on every turn of the event loop. A use case for idle handles is discussed"
" in :doc:`utilities`. Let us use an idle watcher to look at the watcher "
"life cycle and see how ``uv_run()`` will now block because a watcher is "
"present. The idle watcher is stopped when the count is reached and "
"``uv_run()`` exits since no event watchers are active."
msgstr "下面是使用 idle 句柄的一个例子。回调在事件循环的每一轮都会被调用一次。idle 句柄的一个用例在 :doc:`utilities` 中有讨论。让我们使用 idle 监视器来观察监视器的生命周期，看看由于存在监视器，``uv_run()`` 现在会如何阻塞。计数达到后，idle 监视器停止，``uv_run()`` 随之退出，因为此时已经没有处于活动状态的事件监视器了。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:219
msgid "idle-basic/main.c"
msgstr "idle-basic/main.c"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:225
msgid "Storing context"
msgstr "保存上下文"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:227
msgid ""
"In callback based programming style you'll often want to pass some "
"'context' -- application specific information -- between the call site "
"and the callback. All handles and requests have a ``void* data`` member "
"which you can set to the context and cast back in the callback. This is a"
" common pattern used throughout the C library ecosystem. In addition "
"``uv_loop_t`` also has a similar data member."
msgstr "在基于回调的编程风格中，你常常需要在调用点与回调之间传递一些“上下文”——应用特定的信息。所有句柄和请求都有一个 ``void* data`` 成员，你可以把它设置为上下文，并在回调中把它转换回来。这是整个 C 库生态中常用的一种模式。此外，``uv_loop_t`` 也有一个类似的数据成员。"

#: ../../src/guide/basics.rst:236
msgid "Depending on the capacity of the hardware of course."
msgstr "当然，这取决于硬件的能力。"

